  "$description": "Cover palettes for generated digest artwork. Colors are OKLCH; packages/cover converts them to sRGB hex with gamut clamping at build time. Each palette is a flat ground of medium chroma (OKLCH 0.12 or less, so a grid of covers stays easy on the eye), one contrasting figure color (3:1 or better against the ground) and a text color for the date and wordmark (4.5:1 or better against the ground). The quiet field tint and mid shade are derived from ground and figure in packages/cover. Ids are named in digest frontmatter, so they are never renamed or removed; only the colors behind an id change.",
